<title>BELGIUM: EU allows imports of South African horses.</title>
<headline>EU allows imports of South African horses.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will allow imports from South Africa of horses, which are guaranteed to be free of African horse sickness, a European Commission official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The move followed South Africa's introduction of quarantine and other measures to control the fatal disease and protect EU horses.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision is of great importance for the South African and the international horse industry as well as for the South African bid for the Olympic Games in 2004,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>The disease occurred on the Iberian peninsula from 1987-90.</p>
</text>
